            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a generation, then the Hindi for to nurture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: याददाश्त",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "याददाश्त — yāddāśt — \"memory (the power to remember)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बुढ़ापे में दादी की याददाश्त कमज़ोर हो गई है। buṛhāpe meṁ dādī kī yāddāśt kamzor ho gaī hai. In her old age my grandmother's memory has grown weak."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "याददाश्त (yāddāśt) is usually traced to Persian yāddāsht, \"a memorandum, memory\", built on yād, \"remembrance\", and a word for \"holding\": holding things in mind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
